; Field access by name on a data type that has a NULLARY
; constructor. Under the mixed representation (MM-VAL-8) a value of
; `T` may be an immediate tag, and field access emits an unguarded
; load - only `match` emits the immediate-or-address guard. So
; `x.v` on `(E)` passed `check` and died of SIGSEGV at run time.
; docs/memory-model.md MM-VAL-9a; refused since 2026-08-14. On a
; data type whose every constructor is fieldful, field access stays
; legal - tests/stdlib/210-struct-variants.ax exercises that half.
(data T
  (E)
  (N { v : Int }))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let ((x E))
    x.v
  )
)
